data/raw/*
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
!data/**/.gitkeep
# Provenance, not data. The manifest carries URLs, SHA-256 hashes, byte counts,
# download dates and licences for every raw input — no observation from any of them.
# It is the reproducibility spine: without it, a checkout cannot tell which vintage of
# which publication a figure came from. Ruled in, 2026-09-05.
!data/raw/MANIFEST.json
__pycache__/
.venv/
*.parquet
*.h5
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Committed on purpose, against the blanket rules above.
# The EEC test fixture is 51 KB of Licence Ouverte data and is what lets CI run
# the population pipeline with no network (tests/fixtures/README.md).
!tests/fixtures/*.parquet
# Generated, but small and part of the product: the reconciliation report is the
# credibility page (PHASE1_SPEC §5), and the baseline summary is what
# GET /population/baseline serves. Both are regenerated by
# `impots population reconcile`.
!data/processed/baseline_*.json

# ERFS interrupt, E0(3) — belt and braces behind scripts/check_no_data_committed.py.
# The delivery (Quetelet-Progedo/ADISP, millésime 2022, version FPR) lives OUTSIDE this
# tree and is reached through an untracked local config. These patterns exist so that a
# stray copy inside the repository is never staged in the first place; the guard is what
# refuses one that gets past them, and it is the guard that carries the kill tests.
# DATA EXTENSIONS ONLY. The first version of this block was `*erfs*` / `*ERFS*`, which
# ignored `src/impots/erfs/` — the code implementing the protection — and `git add -A`
# then reported success while adding nothing. A guard broad enough to swallow its own
# implementation is not strict, it is broken.
*erfs*.csv
*erfs*.dta
*erfs*.parquet
*erfs*.sav
*erfs*.sas7bdat
*ERFS*.csv
*ERFS*.dta
*ERFS*.parquet
fpr_*.csv
fpr_*.dta
fpr_*.parquet
fpr_*.sav
fpr_*.sas7bdat
lil-1696*
.impots.local
# Owner's ruling (2026-09-18): the delivery's PUBLIC documentation may sit under
# data/raw/, and all of it is ignored. `data/raw/*` at the top of this file already
# covers it; these lines are belt and braces, and they name the extensions the
# documentation actually uses so that a stray .csv or .dta can never ride in behind a
# rule written for PDFs.
data/raw/erfs_*.pdf
data/raw/erfs_*.xlsx
data/raw/erfs_*.txt
data/raw/cerfa_*.pdf

# Sélection par impact et relevé de mémoire (D-309) : ce que chaque test a lu, et sa mémoire.
.cache/
